  {
    "episode_id": 51126,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51126.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 2,
    "turn_text": "My biggest accomplishment is that 16 years later, I still have my principal's integrity and hopefully my reputation intact. That's what I consider to be my greatest accomplishment. Otherwise, I take some pride in the fact that as a team, I believe that particularly in this Congress, we've been able to play a significant role in the regulatory efforts in our financial markets to really promote economic growth, to lift a lot of the common man and woman in particularly The role we played in putting forth the most pro-growth banking bill in a generation, probably since Graham leach, blithely. It wasn't easy. So we had set out to repeal and replace Dodd-Frank. We didn't quite do that, but to quote our president, we did do a number on it. And I think that has",
