  {
    "episode_id": 51126,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51126.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "One of your signature pieces of legislation was the Financial Choice Act, which many would argue was a fairly sweeping rollback of Dodd-Frank, eliminating the Volcker rules, significantly raining in the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, among many other things. I imagine you knew it might have a tough time getting that 60-vote threshold in the Senate. What was your motivation for taking such an aggressive approach?",
