        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker assumes that 'aggressive' policy change is a meaningful descriptor of the Financial Choice Act's scope.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker assumes that rolling back Dodd-Frank regulations is politically consequential and controversial.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker assumes that motivations behind legislation should be evaluated based on intended impact rather than just procedural outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 51126,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51126.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think if you look carefully at my chairmanship and style of leadership, I think it is important that number one, conservatives and Republicans set forth. paradigm pieces of legislation that are comprehensive that encompass our vision of capital markets, of banking, of security markets, of housing. So we want to know what the ultimate goal is, but having said that, Once you put that out there and you know what the goal is, you know that in order to actually pass law and make law and not just make speeches, you're going to have to engage in the legislative process, the give and the take. And if we end up with 20% of what we set out to do, that's probably a pretty good day. And then we'll come back and continue to work on it. But I think you have to be number one. comprehensive in your view, comprehensive in your goals, but work incrementally for positive change. And so some of the matters that I've worked on, we see an immediate result from, I think, other matters that I've worked on and may take a generation. or more before ultimately those goals are realized. So, you know, I've tried to play a long game and tried to play a short game as well. And I think they're both important. I think it is important to have the vision and I think it's important to make progress.",
