    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51126.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "After that bill passed the House, it was time for the Senate to rewrite its own version. We had Chairman Mike Crapow of the Senate Banking Committee as well as some moderate Democrats putting together a more modest regulatory relief bill. I know that was a bill that you wanted to see some changes to. What was your biggest frustration with that process?",
