    "turn_text": "always kept his word. So I have no doubt this will be voted on again. The timing in this Congress is what's a little up in the air. It's his decision. There wasn't a firm commitment on timing. There was a firm commitment that we would receive a vote. I am still hopeful, optimistic that a vote will take place prior to the election. The Senate, believe it or not, can't you gum and walk at the same time as they are embroiled in this incredible controversy over the Supreme Court nomination. They are also passing appropriations bill and I think we'll soon a rather strong bipartisan opioid bill, that opioid prevention treatment bill that came out of the house. Well, our capital formation bill came out of the House of 40624. I'm not sure we could have a Mother's Day resolution come out of the House of 40624. There's no reason why this shouldn't go to the Senate and go soon. Listen, if Maxine Waters and I can see eye to eye on seeing this through, this ought to be the least controversial bill that Senate takes up. Having said that, it still does a lot of good things for our startups. for entrepreneurial activity to combat China on their expropriation of our technology to encourage high-tech companies and companies with valuable intellectual property to go public in the US as opposed to offshore. There's a lot of really good capital formation and some banking legislation that was left on the cutting room floor in 2155. in this bill. So I've encouraged all my friends in the Senate. I still think I can claim a few to take this bill up sooner as opposed to later.",
