    "turn_text": "Well, I used the term earlier. I never say never, but it is not my desire to stay in this town. It is not my desire to have another government job. I've got two teenagers in the nest throughout the entirety of their life. I have been a part-time father. I would like to be a full-time father. And these are important years. So clearly the catalyst for leaving is the term limit, but the real reason for leaving, nobody believes you in this town, but the real reason for leaving is my family. When I went to my first grand, my daughter was in my arms and my son didn't exist. Now she's dating and driving and he has a peach fuzz mustache and I've been a part-time dad the whole time. They may always be on the family payroll, but they're not always going to be in the nest. So I feel strongly that I want to go home Otherwise, I'm putting off my future. I'll talk to people once the new Congress is sworn in. Meanwhile, we have business to be done, and I want to avoid any conflicts of interest. So a couple of people have come up to me and asked me what I'm doing. And I said, well, come the first week of January, we'll have that conversation.",
